{"model": "gpt-oss-120b", "input": [{"role": "developer", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "Review the complete supplied SHACL against source, schema and declared research scope. Return one JSON object matching expected_response_schema. Review every query/branch and all represented source obligations. No fixtures, labels, counterpart records, expected verdicts or known solution are supplied. Never request them. Shape messages and execution success are not proofs of correct logic.\n\nThe packet supplies full_candidate once. Use candidate_location rather than quoting code: {candidate_version, candidate_sha256, unit: \"lines\" or \"characters\", start, end}. Lines are one-based inclusive; character offsets are zero-based half-open Unicode positions. The server extracts exact code. Reference previous_location against previous_candidate when assessing changes. For missing code, locate a real insertion anchor. Never invent ranges or stale hashes.\n\nEvidence uses concise request-local E IDs. The server binds each to immutable content and provenance hashes. Use only IDs in this packet. source_evidence_id must identify a SOURCE entry; source_excerpt, when asserted, must be an exact nonempty substring preserving source whitespace. evidence_id/evidence_excerpt must match supplied text; RDF_FACT permits only one equivalent explicit ground triple with identical RDF terms, lexical forms, datatype and language. No inference, numeric coercion, blank-node equivalence or ontology-wide lookup. A valid reference does not prove the interpretation. Caller admission is an experimental assumption with provenance, not a legal-source quotation or independently certified eligibility.\n\nDecisions: ACCEPT (no issues, all changes supported and prior issues resolved); REJECT (actionable source/schema-backed code issue); UNRESOLVED (material missing information); REQUEST_EVIDENCE (up to three bounded catalog source/schema requests). Unsupported claims, uncertainty and absent evidence must remain explicit. For every material retrieval gap include unchecked {scope: gap_id, material, reason}. Material unchecked scope prevents ACCEPT. Activation/deactivation and full query correctness are separate obligations; resolving scope proves neither arithmetic nor compliance.\n\nFor each functional change_id return ONE change_assessments entry, with source support, current/previous locations and reason. If removal_required is true, removal_disposition must be SUPPORTED_REMOVAL, REPLACED, REGRESSION or UNRESOLVED and the reason must assess lost numeric/unit/query/target obligations and any replacement. There is no separate removal response list or pre-issued repair permission. Source-supported removal of an excessive old restriction is allowed; checker silence alone is not support. REGRESSION/UNRESOLVED requires a corresponding issue/change_id; UNRESOLVED requires an unresolved-context issue and decision.\n\nReconcile exactly the original prior_issues IDs; code edits alone do not resolve an issue. Empty prior_issues requires empty reconciliations. Format feedback does not create accepted issues or authorize repair; the original candidate/prior state and request binding remain unchanged. Echo candidate_version, candidate_sha256 and review_request_id. Correct all listed format errors in a complete response.\n\nUse proposed_path_role PROPERTY for a path ending at the named property, NUMERIC_OPERAND for traversal through that quantity property to the declared numeric predicate. Do not concatenate unrelated owner branches or relabel units as conversion. Vocabulary/domain/range facts do not alone establish ownership or legal eligibility.\n\nexecution_probe is an actual candidate-bound engine observation, with full logs preserved in server artifacts. A static translation/binding warning is not a confirmed engine failure. Successful execution does not establish complete branch coverage or regulatory adequacy. Nested/library shapes need no target if reachable from an active root. Material unsupported activation, deactivation or unknown bindings prevent acceptance. Never invent selectors, target fixture identities, infer eligibility from missing data or weaken source obligations to silence diagnostics.\n\n\nResponse correction and operand pairing: An issue about several operands may use operands[], each with a unique operand_id and its own property, proposed_path and explicit proposed_path_role (PROPERTY or NUMERIC_OPERAND); optional proposed_unit/proposed_datatype belong to that operand. The same declared representation evidence applies. Legacy scalar proposals are still checked and are not discarded when operands are present. Never pair one property's name with another property's path.\n\nA proven internal pairing inconsistency may return exact validation_errors using the existing shared response-correction allowance. Correct or withdraw the inconsistent proposal; do not rewrite the candidate. Keep original candidate, evidence and prior issues unchanged. Rejected response issues are not prior state. An unknown path or genuine source/schema contradiction remains blocking: report representation_disposition UNRESOLVED_CONTRADICTION (and uncertainty), never disguise a contradiction as formatting. Evidence citations do not prove an interpretation. No requirement-specific calculation answer is supplied.\n"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "input_text", "text": "{\"candidate_version\": 2, \"candidate_sha256\": \"8299aa76a8545444f27e97d1ba8598fbf006401131624d640c78f1c400a91ea0\", \"review_request_id\": \"review:a13cb1b262706735aed0ee8f979701b0fdc45056ffd75b0161caafff03541de0\", \"full_candidate\": \"@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Shape for QuantityValue (the representation of a numeric quantity)\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nnltl:QuantityValueShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    # NOTE: No global targetClass – activation is limited to contexts where the shape is referenced via sh:node.\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\\n        sh:message \\\"A QuantityValue must have exactly one numericValue (decimal).\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\\n        sh:class unit:KiloTON_Metric ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\\n        sh:message \\\"A QuantityValue must specify the unit KiloTON_Metric (kt).\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    sh:message \\\"A QuantityValue representing displacement must have a decimal numericValue and unit kt.\\\" .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Shape for upperIceWaterlineCase (design condition)\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nnltl:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    # NOTE: No global targetClass – the shape is applied via sh:node from the Ship shape.\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path nltl:waterlineCaseDisplacement ;\\n        sh:node nltl:QuantityValueShape ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:message \\\"Each UpperIceWaterlineCase must have a waterlineCaseDisplacement expressed as a QuantityValue.\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    sh:message \\\"UpperIceWaterlineCase must provide displacement for the associated waterline case.\\\" .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Shape for Ship (the primary focus class)\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nnltl:ShipShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\\n    # Requirement: ship must be linked to at least one UpperIceWaterlineCase\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path nltl:hasUpperIceWaterlineCase ;\\n        sh:class nltl:upperIceWaterlineCase ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:node nltl:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape ;\\n        sh:message \\\"A ship must have at least one UpperIceWaterlineCase (hasUpperIceWaterlineCase).\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    # Requirement: ship displacement (DUI) expressed as upperIceWaterlineDisplacement\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path nltl:upperIceWaterlineDisplacement ;\\n        sh:node nltl:QuantityValueShape ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:message \\\"A ship must have an upperIceWaterlineDisplacement (DUI) expressed as a QuantityValue.\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    # NOTE: The UR I2.1.2.2 specifies that when multiple waterlines exist,\\n    # the displacement used must be the greatest among them.  SHACL does\\n    # not provide a native mechanism to compute a maximum across a set of\\n    # values; therefore this aspect of the requirement is recorded as\\n    # ambiguous and is not enforced by the shape.  Implementations may\\n    # apply additional SPARQL-based SHACL constraints if required.\\n    sh:message \\\"Ship must be linked to an UpperIceWaterlineCase and provide its displacement (DUI) in kt.\\\" .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Documentation of ambiguity\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n_:ambiguityNote\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    rdfs:comment \\\"Ambiguity: The requirement 'where multiple waterlines are used, the displacement is to be determined from the waterline corresponding to the greatest displacement' cannot be fully expressed in pure SHACL.  The shape therefore enforces the existence of the relevant properties but does not enforce the 'greatest displacement' selection rule.\\\" .\\n\", \"previous_candidate\": {\"version\": 1, \"sha256\": \"db559ab3c423e96c914ff3120cac52174fbc9d3a7d7b966953fadc90a918c804\", \"full_code\": \"@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\\n@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Shape for QuantityValue (the representation of a numeric quantity)\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nnltl:QuantityValueShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue ;\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\\n        sh:message \\\"A QuantityValue must have exactly one numericValue (decimal).\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\\n        sh:class unit:KiloTON_Metric ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\\n        sh:message \\\"A QuantityValue must specify the unit KiloTON_Metric (kt).\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    sh:message \\\"A QuantityValue representing displacement must have a decimal numericValue and unit kt.\\\" .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Shape for upperIceWaterlineCase (design condition)\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nnltl:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    sh:targetClass nltl:upperIceWaterlineCase ;\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path nltl:waterlineCaseDisplacement ;\\n        sh:node nltl:QuantityValueShape ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:message \\\"Each UpperIceWaterlineCase must have a waterlineCaseDisplacement expressed as a QuantityValue.\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    sh:message \\\"UpperIceWaterlineCase must provide displacement for the associated waterline case.\\\" .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Shape for Ship (the primary focus class)\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\nnltl:ShipShape\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\\n    # Requirement: ship must be linked to at least one UpperIceWaterlineCase\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path nltl:hasUpperIceWaterlineCase ;\\n        sh:class nltl:upperIceWaterlineCase ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:node nltl:UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape ;\\n        sh:message \\\"A ship must have at least one UpperIceWaterlineCase (hasUpperIceWaterlineCase).\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    # Requirement: ship displacement (DUI) expressed as upperIceWaterlineDisplacement\\n    sh:property [\\n        sh:path nltl:upperIceWaterlineDisplacement ;\\n        sh:node nltl:QuantityValueShape ;\\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:message \\\"A ship must have an upperIceWaterlineDisplacement (DUI) expressed as a QuantityValue.\\\" ;\\n    ] ;\\n    # NOTE: The UR I2.1.2.2 specifies that when multiple waterlines exist,\\n    # the displacement used must be the greatest among them.  SHACL does\\n    # not provide a native mechanism to compute a maximum across a set of\\n    # values; therefore this aspect of the requirement is recorded as\\n    # ambiguous and is not enforced by the shape.  Implementations may\\n    # apply additional SPARQL-based SHACL constraints if required.\\n    sh:message \\\"Ship must be linked to an UpperIceWaterlineCase and provide its displacement (DUI) in kt.\\\" .\\n\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n# Documentation of ambiguity\\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\\n _:ambiguityNote\\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\\n    rdfs:comment \\\"Ambiguity: The requirement 'where multiple waterlines are used, the displacement is to be determined from the waterline corresponding to the greatest displacement' cannot be fully expressed in pure SHACL.  The shape therefore enforces the existence of the relevant properties but does not enforce the 'greatest displacement' selection rule.\\\" .\\n\"}, \"max_issues\": 12, \"expected_response_schema\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"candidate_version\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"candidate_sha256\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"review_request_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"decision\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"ACCEPT\", \"REJECT\", \"UNRESOLVED\", \"REQUEST_EVIDENCE\"]}, \"issues\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"issue_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"SOURCE_BACKED_LOGIC_ERROR\", \"UNRESOLVED_CONTEXT\"]}, \"source_clause\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source_evidence_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source_excerpt\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"expected\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"suggestion\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"evidence_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"evidence_excerpt\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"change_id\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}, \"property\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}, \"proposed_unit\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}, \"proposed_datatype\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}, \"proposed_path\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}, \"candidate_location\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"candidate_version\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"candidate_sha256\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"characters\", \"lines\"]}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"candidate_version\", \"candidate_sha256\", \"unit\", \"start\", \"end\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"proposed_path_role\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"enum\": [\"PROPERTY\", \"NUMERIC_OPERAND\", null]}, \"operands\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1, \"maxItems\": 8, \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"operand_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"property\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"proposed_path\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1, \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"proposed_path_role\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"PROPERTY\", \"NUMERIC_OPERAND\"]}, \"proposed_unit\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}, \"proposed_datatype\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}}, \"required\": [\"operand_id\", \"property\", \"proposed_path\", \"proposed_path_role\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}, \"representation_disposition\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"enum\": [\"USE_DECLARED_REPRESENTATION\", \"UNRESOLVED_CONTRADICTION\", null]}}, \"required\": [\"issue_id\", \"category\", \"source_clause\", \"source_evidence_id\", \"source_excerpt\", \"reason\", \"expected\", \"suggestion\", \"evidence_id\", \"evidence_excerpt\", \"candidate_location\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"maxItems\": 12}, \"change_assessments\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"change_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"disposition\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"SUPPORTED\", \"REGRESSION\", \"UNRESOLVED\"]}, \"source_evidence_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source_excerpt\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"candidate_location\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"candidate_version\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"candidate_sha256\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"characters\", \"lines\"]}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"candidate_version\", \"candidate_sha256\", \"unit\", \"start\", \"end\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"previous_location\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"candidate_version\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"candidate_sha256\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"characters\", \"lines\"]}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"candidate_version\", \"candidate_sha256\", \"unit\", \"start\", \"end\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"removal_disposition\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"], \"enum\": [\"SUPPORTED_REMOVAL\", \"REPLACED\", \"REGRESSION\", \"UNRESOLVED\", null]}}, \"required\": [\"change_id\", \"disposition\", \"source_evidence_id\", \"source_excerpt\", \"reason\", \"candidate_location\", \"previous_location\", \"removal_disposition\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"reconciliations\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"issue_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"state\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"RESOLVED\", \"PERSISTENT\", \"REGRESSED\", \"UNASSESSABLE\"]}, \"source_evidence_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source_excerpt\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"candidate_location\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"candidate_version\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"candidate_sha256\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"characters\", \"lines\"]}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"candidate_version\", \"candidate_sha256\", \"unit\", \"start\", \"end\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"required\": [\"issue_id\", \"state\", \"source_evidence_id\", \"source_excerpt\", \"reason\", \"candidate_location\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"unchecked\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"scope\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"material\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"scope\", \"material\", \"reason\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"evidence_requests\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"maxItems\": 3, \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"kind\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"source\", \"schema\"]}, \"reference\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}, \"section\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]}, \"revision\": {\"type\": [\"integer\", \"null\"]}, \"query\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"kind\", \"query\", \"reason\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"context_assessments\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"finding_key\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"disposition\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"REPAIRABLE_CODE\", \"MISSING_INFORMATION\", \"UNRESOLVED\"]}, \"source_evidence_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source_excerpt\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"evidence_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"evidence_excerpt\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"candidate_location\": {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {\"candidate_version\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"candidate_sha256\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"unit\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"characters\", \"lines\"]}, \"start\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}, \"end\": {\"type\": \"integer\"}}, \"required\": [\"candidate_version\", \"candidate_sha256\", \"unit\", \"start\", \"end\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}, \"required\": [\"finding_key\", \"disposition\", \"source_evidence_id\", \"source_excerpt\", \"evidence_id\", \"evidence_excerpt\", \"reason\", \"candidate_location\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}}}, \"required\": [\"candidate_version\", \"candidate_sha256\", \"review_request_id\", \"decision\", \"issues\", \"change_assessments\", \"reconciliations\", \"unchecked\"], \"additionalProperties\": false}, \"execution_probe\": {\"candidate_version\": 2, \"candidate_sha256\": \"8299aa76a8545444f27e97d1ba8598fbf006401131624d640c78f1c400a91ea0\", \"engine\": \"pyshacl\", \"engine_version\": \"0.31.0\", \"engine_outcome\": \"COMPLETED_NO_ENGINE_ERROR\", \"diagnostic_availability\": \"Captured verbatim\", \"activation\": {\"roots\": [\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ShipShape\"], \"reachable\": [\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#QuantityValueShape\", \"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ShipShape\", \"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#UpperIceWaterlineCaseShape\", \"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b1\", \"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b2\", \"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b3\", \"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b4\", \"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b5\"], \"enforcing_nodes\": [\"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b1\", \"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b2\", \"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b3\", \"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b4\", \"n5155f2415a6b4b1b9dedb6664a58efa9b5\"], \"deactivated_reachable\": [], \"orphan_constraint_nodes\": [], \"unsupported_custom_targets\": [], \"supported\": true}, \"regulatory_correctness_established\": false, \"scope\": \"Execution-only schema-derived probe; no expected regulatory verdict; success is not complete correctness\", \"diagnostics\": {\"stdout\": {\"sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\", \"characters\": 0, \"artifact_field\": \"execution_probe.exact_diagnostics.stdout\"}, \"stderr\": {\"sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855\", \"characters\": 0, \"artifact_field\": \"execution_probe.exact_diagnostics.stderr\"}}}, \"citation_format\": {\"source\": \"source_evidence_id + source_excerpt: verbatim nonempty substring of that SOURCE text; preserve whitespace\", \"schema\": \"evidence_id + evidence_excerpt: exact substring of referenced text. RDF_FACT permits a single equivalent Turtle/N-Triples fact with exact RDF terms only.\", \"code\": \"candidate_location / previous_location: {candidate_version, candidate_sha256, unit: lines|characters, start, end}; lines are inclusive one-based, Unicode character offsets half-open zero-based. Exact code is extracted server-side; do not reproduce indentation.\", \"state\": \"Echo candidate_version, candidate_sha256 and review_request_id. Reconcile only IDs in original prior_issues. Failed review output is not state.\", \"limits\": \"Do not cite arbitrary ontology facts, unsupplied context, inference or numeric-value equivalence as RDF identity.\"}, \"protocol_version\": 2, \"context\": {\"requirement\": {\"id\": \"I2-004\", \"source\": \"UR I2 Structural Requirements for Polar Class Ships\", \"clause\": \"I2.1.2.2\"}, \"scope\": \"Implement and review the supplied source in the declared schema. No supplied compliance solution or expected verdict. Material unspecified representation/applicability prevents acceptance. External population/date eligibility and edition selection are supplied by caller admission, not independently inferred from RDF. Conditions within the represented requirement remain in scope; activation and query correctness are separate obligations.\", \"source_selection\": {\"manifest_sha256\": \"36c8b4e14715ec0e62f77b4d278a08ee5776a42ff869d433d66a8afb2beef41d\", \"included_characters\": 2448, \"original_characters\": 62501, \"omitted_sections\": 108, \"retrieval\": \"Schema.source_evidence(file, document_sha256, start, end); complete sections/hashes retained in source_selection_manifest.json; missing necessary evidence must remain unresolved\"}, \"source_completeness\": \"Deterministic source selection, not a proof of complete context. Ambiguous primary anchors retain full source; unresolved references require review.\"}, \"admission_sha256\": \"6f86aab3cdfe221af8c0524fbb478cbc3a1242bde9c7a564a9153091f50d3dae\", \"evidence_catalog\": {\"format_version\": 2, \"catalog_sha256\": \"1ccd96b3251a8a28cd47967bc06d3bc6251300fd8bcfc9d4c360c719534ebbfb\", \"entries\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"E1\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraught> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#stage1LocalName> \\\"upperIceWaterlineDraught\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E2\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#usedToReachLowerIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Used to reach lower ice waterline\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E3\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCenteredPosition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Not a quantity property\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E4\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#usedToReachLowerIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Used to reach lower ice waterline\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E5\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for upperIceWaterline derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E6\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-013\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E7\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterlineReferencePosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Lower ice waterline reference position\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E8\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"         I2.13   Longitudinal strength\\n\\n         I2.13.1 Application\\n\\n         I2.13.1.1 A ramming impact on the bow is the design scenario for the evaluation of the\\n         longitudinal strength of the hull.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n                                                       I2-17                       IACS Req. 2006/Rev.4 2019\\n\\f                                                                                                            I2\\n\\n\\n         I2.13.1.2 Intentional ramming is not considered as a design scenario for ships which are\\nI2       designed with vertical or bulbous bows, see I1.1.6. Hence the longitudinal strength\\n(cont)   requirements given in I2.13 is not to be considered for ships with stem angle stem equal to or\\n         larger than 80 deg.\\n\\n         I2.13.1.3 Ice loads are only to be combined with still water loads. The combined stresses\\n         are to be compared against permissible bending and shear stresses at different locations\\n         along the ship’s length. In addition, sufficient local buckling strength is also to be verified.\\n\\n         I2.13.2 Design vertical ice force at the bow\\n\\n         I2.13.2.1 The design vertical ice force at the bow, FIB, is to be taken as\\n\\n         FIB = minimum (FIB,1; FIB,2) [MN]\\n\\n             where FIB,1 = 0.534 ꞏ KI0.15 ꞏ sin0.2(stem) ꞏ (DUI ꞏ Kh)0.5 ꞏ CFL [MN]\\n\\n                     FIB,2 = 1.20 ꞏ CFF [MN]\\n\\n                      KI = indentation parameter = Kf / Kh\\n                      a) for the case of a blunt bow form\\n                        Kf = (2 ꞏ C ꞏ BUI1-eb / (1 + eb))0.9 ꞏ tan(stem)-0.9ꞏ(1 + eb)\\n                      b) for the case of wedge bow form (stem < 80 deg), eb =1 and the above simplifies to\\n                        Kf = (tan(stem) / tan2(stem))0.9\\n                      Kh = 0.01 ꞏ Awp [MN/m]\\n                      CFL = Longitudinal Strength Class Factor from Table 1\\n                      eb = bow shape exponent which best describes the waterplane (see Figures 7\\n                      and 8)\\n                          = 1.0 for a simple wedge bow form\\n                          = 0.4 to 0.6 for a spoon bow form\\n                          = 0 for a landing craft bow form\\n                      An approximate eb determined by a simple fit is acceptable\\n                 stem = stem angle to be measured between the horizontal axis and the stem\\n                        tangent at the upper ice waterline [deg] (buttock angle as per Figure 2 measured\\n                        on the centreline)\\n                      stem = waterline angle measured in way of the stem at the upper ice waterline\\n                        (UIWL) [deg] (see Figure 7)\\n                      C = 1 / (2 ꞏ (LB / BUI)eb)\\n                      BUI = moulded breadth corresponding to the upper ice waterline (UIWL) [m]\\n                      LB = bow length used in the equation y = BUI / 2 ꞏ (x/LB)eb [m] (see Figures 7 and 8)\\n                      DUI = displacement as defined in I2.1.2.2, not to be taken less than 10 [kt]\\n                      Awp = waterplane area corresponding to the upper ice waterline (UIWL) [m2]\\n                      CFF = Flexural Failure Class Factor from Table 1\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n                                                  I2-18                    IACS Req. 2006/Rev.4 2019\\n\\f                                                                                                       I2\\n\\n\\n                                        Figure 7 - Bow shape definition\\nI2\\n(cont)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n                Figure 8 - Illustration of eb effect on the bow shape for BUI = 20 and LB =16\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/IACS_I2_full.txt\", \"edition\": \"Rev.4 (December 2019)\", \"authority\": \"IACS\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 50184, \"end\": 53761, \"line_start\": 940, \"line_end\": 1017, \"page_start\": 17, \"page_end\": 19}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E9\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-011\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E10\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-B01-097\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E11\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"To qualify for ice class IA Super, IA, IB or IC, a ship the keel of which is laid or which is at a similar stage of construction on or after 1 September 2003 shall comply with the following requirements regarding its engine output. The engine output requirement shall be calculated for two draughts by formula 3.1. Draughts to be used are the maximum draught a...\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E12\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Design condition\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E13\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#displacementAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#roleDecisionBasis> \\\"Quantity metadata requires the canonical QUDT QuantityValue node pattern\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E14\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCase> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"I2-004\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E15\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipDisplacementFactor> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#recommendedUnit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E16\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#usedToReachLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-B01-238\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E17\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraught> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitSymbol> \\\"m\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E18\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E19\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLength> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Recommended canonical QUDT unit selected by Stage 2 engineering normalization: Canonical benchmark length unit\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E20\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#roleDecisionBasis> \\\"Typed relationship needed to traverse between engineering or evidence nodes.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E21\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceReference> \\\"IMO26-002 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.2 | Chapter 9-1 applicability; IMO26-016 | IMO_AMEND_2026 p.5 | Chapter 11-1 applicability\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E22\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-066\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E23\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Upper ice waterline displacement\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E24\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"The upper ice waterline (UIWL) shall be the envelope of the highest points of the waterlines at which the ship is intended to operate in ice. The line may be a broken line.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E25\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Verified recommended QUDT unit from Stage 1 or a documented Stage 2 source-unit refinement\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E26\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#framingIceStrengtheningAboveUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Framing ice strengthening above upper ice waterline\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E27\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitSymbol> \\\"kW\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E28\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceAlias> \\\"LIWL\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E29\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraughtDUI> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#recommendedUnit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E30\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCase> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E31\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Minimum required power at upper ice waterline\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E32\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#displacementAtUpperIceWaterline\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"QuantityProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Displacement at upper ice waterline\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"displacementAtUpperIceWaterline\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"TRF-016 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/TON_Metric\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"t\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E33\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E34\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceAlias> \\\"P_min_LIWL_kW\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E35\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterlineReferencePosition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Applicable TRAFICOM regulation wording plus explicit engineering node/operand role\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E36\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Benchmark entity\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E37\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingRule> \\\"N1 - reuse only after exact URI and semantic-context verification\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E38\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#displacementAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-0213\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E39\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#framingIceStrengtheningAboveUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Applicable TRAFICOM regulation wording plus explicit engineering node/operand role\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E40\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E41\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO26-016\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E42\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-016\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E43\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceReference> \\\"I2-003 | IACS_UR_I2 p.1 | I2.1.2.1; I2-004 | IACS_UR_I2 p.1 | I2.1.2.2; TRF-011 | TRAFICOM p.6 | 2.1; TRF-014 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-015 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-016 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-020 | TRAFICOM p.8-9 | 3.2.2; TRF-030 | TRAFICOM p.12 | 4.1; TRF-061 | TRAFICOM p.25 | 4.7\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E44\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-020\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E45\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-0270\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E46\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#situatedAboveLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-B01-215\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E47\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Upper ice waterline case\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E48\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#stage1LocalName> \\\"cargoShip\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E49\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"ObjectProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Has upper ice waterline case\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"hasUpperIceWaterlineCase\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCase\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"I2-004 | IACS_UR_I2 p.1 | I2.1.2.2\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E50\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineBreadth> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E51\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraught> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E52\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLengthLUI> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Upper ice waterline length l u i\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E53\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#displacementAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"The ship shall always be loaded down at least to the draught of LIWL amidships when navigating in ice. Any ballast tank, situated above the LIWL and needed to load down the ship to this water line, shall be equipped with devices to prevent the water from freezing. In determining the LIWL, regard shall be paid to the need to ensure a reasonable degree of ice-...\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E54\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtLowerIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E55\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLengthLUI> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-R9-0335\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E56\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineBreadth> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingRule> \\\"N4 - explicit engineering quantity in ASCII lowerCamelCase; formula symbols remain aliases only.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E57\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraughtDUI> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (R9 development): Upper ice waterline draught d u i represents the linked requirement entity, relationship, value, evidence role, or quantity; its scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E58\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraughtDUI\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"QuantityProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Upper ice waterline draught d u i\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"upperIceWaterlineDraughtDUI\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"I2-050 | IACS_UR_I2 p.18 | I2.13.2.1\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"m\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E59\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-012\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E60\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E61\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (R9 development): Upper ice waterline case represents the linked requirement entity, relationship, value, evidence role, or quantity; its scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E62\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"IMO26-016\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E63\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraught> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"The ice damage extents to be assumed when demonstrating compliance with paragraph 4.3.2.1 shall be such that: the longitudinal extent is 4.5% of the upper ice waterline length if centred forward of the maximum breadth on the upper ice waterline, and 1.5% of upper ice waterline length otherwise, and shall be assumed at any longitudinal position along the ship...\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E64\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#module> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#moduleHull> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E65\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#designCondition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E66\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#brashIceChannelResistanceAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-020\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E67\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#oilTanker> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"For category A and B ships other than oil tankers constructed on or after 1 January 2017, all cargo tanks constructed and utilized to carry oil shall be separated from the outer shell by a distance of not less than 0.76 m.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E68\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for upperIceWaterlineLength derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E69\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterlineCase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Has upper ice waterline case\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E70\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#brashIceChannelResistanceAtUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E71\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Pleasure yacht\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E72\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (R9 development): Upper ice waterline displacement represents the linked requirement entity, relationship, value, evidence role, or quantity; its scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E73\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#framingIceStrengtheningAboveUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-043\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E74\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"xsd:boolean\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#situatedAboveLowerIceWaterline\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"DatatypeProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Situated above lower ice waterline\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"situatedAboveLowerIceWaterline\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"TRF-016 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E75\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E76\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterlineReferencePosition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-DEV-B01-152\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E77\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Not a quantity property\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E78\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineReferencePosition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Upper ice waterline reference position\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E79\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#usedToReachLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingRule> \\\"N4 - explicit regulatory concept in ASCII lowerCamelCase with an XSD datatype.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E80\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterline\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"ObjectProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Has upper ice waterline\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"hasUpperIceWaterline\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceWaterline\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"TRF-011 | TRAFICOM p.6 | 2.1; TRF-013 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-016 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-020 | TRAFICOM p.8-9 | 3.2.2\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E81\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#brashIceChannelResistanceAtUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Brash ice channel resistance at upper ice waterline\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E82\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraught> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceAlias> \\\"upper_ice_waterline_draught\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E83\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"                                                                                                           I2\\n\\n\\n\\nI2          Structural Requirements for Polar Class Ships\\n(August\\n(cont)\\n2006)       I2.1 General\\n(Rev.1\\nJan 2007)   I2.1.1 Application*\\n(Corr.1\\nOct 2007)   This UR applies to Polar Class ships according to UR I1.\\n(Rev.2\\nNov 2010)   I2.1.2 Definitions\\n(Rev.3\\nApr 2016)   I2.1.2.1 The length LUI is the distance, in m, measured horizontally from the fore side of the\\n(Rev.4      stem at the intersection with the upper ice waterline (UIWL) to the after side of the rudder\\nDec 2019)   post, or the centre of the rudder stock if there is no rudder post. LUI is not to be less than\\n            96%, and need not be greater than 97%, of the extreme length of the upper ice waterline\\n            (UIWL) measured horizontally from the fore side of the stem. In ships with unusual stern and\\n            bow arrangement the length LUI will be specially considered.\\n\\n            I2.1.2.2 The ship displacement DUI is the displacement, in kt, of the ship corresponding to the\\n            upper ice waterline (UIWL). Where multiple waterlines are used for determining the UIWL, the\\n            displacement is to be determined from the waterline corresponding to the greatest\\n            displacement.\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/IACS_I2_full.txt\", \"authority\": \"User-supplied retained source document; interpretations are not independently verified\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 0, \"end\": 1304}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E84\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#usedToReachLowerIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Batch 01 development): Used to reach lower ice waterline is the benchmark representation of the linked requirement operand, relationship, evidence role, or controlled value. Exact scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E85\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E86\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLength> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#evidenceExcerpt> \\\"The ice damage extents to be assumed when demonstrating compliance with paragraph 4.3.2.1 shall be such that: the longitudinal extent is 4.5% of the upper ice waterline length if centred forward of the maximum breadth on the upper ice waterline, and 1.5% of upper ice waterline length otherwise, and shall be assumed at any longitudinal position along the ship...\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E87\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineBreadth> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceWaterline> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E88\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineBreadth> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Upper ice waterline breadth\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E89\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E90\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#oilTanker> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Oil tanker\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E91\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterlineReferencePosition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingRule> \\\"N4 - explicit engineering quantity in ASCII lowerCamelCase; formula symbols remain aliases only.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E92\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate concept for passengerShip derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E93\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDisplacement> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#recommendedUnit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTON_Metric> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E94\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#waterlineCaseDisplacement> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#recommendedUnit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloTON_Metric> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E95\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"[{\\\"binding_search_truncated\\\": true, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"schema\\\", \\\"meaning\\\": \\\"Vocabulary/type/domain/range existence is not evidence of legal eligibility or of an applicability binding. Other-requirement mappings cannot be transferred automatically.\\\", \\\"query_sha256\\\": \\\"79d24f684beec7ebdce7e2d8ed033f25fb43091eb3365ae31a9a74d1cd2594f8\\\", \\\"representation_mappings\\\": [{\\\"model_paths\\\": [{\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"bowSubregionCalculationCase\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"bowFormApplicabilityValue\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"bowFormApplicabilityClassification\\\"}, {\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"bowSubregionCalculationCase\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasBowSubregionCalculationCase\\\"}, {\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"bowSubregionCalculationCase\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"tableLookupCase\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasFailureClassFactorLookupCase\\\"}], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"upperIceWaterlineLengthLUI\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"I2-015\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": null}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [{\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"nonBowIceLoadCalculationCase\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasNonBowIceLoadCalculationCase\\\"}], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"shipDisplacementFactor\\\": \\\"nonBowIceLoadCalculationCase\\\", \\\"upperIceWaterlineDraughtDUI\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"I2-017\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": null}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"upperIceWaterlineDraughtDUI\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"I2-050\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": null}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"upperIceWaterlineLengthLUI\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"I2-051\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": null}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [{\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"calculationCase\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasCalculationCase\\\"}, {\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"hullGirderBendingMomentCalculationCase\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasHullGirderBendingMomentCalculationCase\\\"}, {\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"calculationCase\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"interpolationPoint\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasInterpolationPoint\\\"}], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"upperIceWaterlineLengthLUI\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"I2-054\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": null}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"hasUpperIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"iceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"TRF-011\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [{\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"iceWaterline\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasIntendedIceOperatingWaterline\\\"}, {\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"iceWaterline\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasLowerIceWaterline\\\"}, {\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"iceWaterline\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"waterlineProfilePoint\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasWaterlineProfilePoint\\\"}], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"hasLowerIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"iceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"TRF-012\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"hasLowerIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"hasUpperIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"TRF-013\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [{\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"classCertificate\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasClassCertificate\\\"}, {\\\"fromOwner\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"toOwner\\\": \\\"iceDraughtRestrictionDocument\\\", \\\"via\\\": \\\"hasIceDraughtRestrictionDocument\\\"}], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"upperIceWaterlineDraught\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"TRF-014\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"upperIceWaterlineDraught\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"TRF-015\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"displacementAtUpperIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"hasLowerIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"hasUpperIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"situatedAboveLowerIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ballastTank\\\", \\\"usedToReachLowerIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ballastTank\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"TRF-016\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}, {\\\"model_paths\\\": [], \\\"owners\\\": {\\\"brashIceChannelResistanceAtUpperIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"hasLowerIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"hasUpperIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"iceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"minimumRequiredPowerAtLowerIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline\\\": \\\"ship\\\", \\\"upperIceWaterlineBreadth\\\": \\\"iceWaterline\\\", \\\"upperIceWaterlineLength\\\": \\\"iceWaterline\\\"}, \\\"requirement_id\\\": \\\"TRF-020\\\", \\\"scope\\\": \\\"OTHER_REQUIREMENT_NOT_TRANSFERABLE\\\", \\\"target_owner\\\": \\\"ship\\\"}], \\\"status\\\": \\\"RETRIEVED\\\", \\\"term_iris\\\": [\\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraughtDUI\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#displacementAtUpperIceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#usedToReachLowerIceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineReferencePosition\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLengthLUI\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLength\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraught\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineCenteredPosition\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineBreadth\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#framingIceStrengtheningAboveUpperIceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#brashIceChannelResistanceAtUpperIceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#situatedAboveLowerIceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipDisplacementFactor\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtLowerIceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterlineReferencePosition\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceWaterline\\\", \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasLowerIceWaterline\\\"]}]\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"retrieved_schema_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E96\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipDisplacementFactor\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"QuantityProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Ship displacement factor\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"shipDisplacementFactor\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"I2-017 | IACS_UR_I2 p.6 | I2.3.2.2\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/UNITLESS\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"1\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E97\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#fishingVessel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Fishing vessel\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E98\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLengthLUI> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#recommendedUnit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E99\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E100\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"                                                                                                          I1\\n\\n\\n\\nI1        Polar Class Descriptions and Application\\n(August\\n(cont)\\n2006)\\n(Rev.1    I1.1     Application\\nJan\\n2007)     I1.1.1 The Unified Requirements for Polar Class ships apply to ships constructed of steel\\n(Corr.1   and intended for independent navigation in ice-infested polar waters.\\nOct\\n2007)     I1.1.2 Ships that comply with the UR I2 and UR I3 can be considered for a Polar Class\\n(Rev.2    notation as listed in Table 1. The requirements of UR I2 and UR I3 are in addition to the open\\nApr       water requirements of the Classification Society. If the hull and machinery are constructed\\n2016)     such as to comply with the requirements of different Polar Classes, then both the hull and\\n          machinery are to be assigned the lower of these classes in the Certificate of Classification.\\n          Compliance of the hull or machinery with the requirements of a higher Polar Class is also to\\n          be indicated in the Certificate of Classification or equivalent.\\n\\n          I1.1.3 Ships which are assigned a Polar Class notation and complying with the relevant\\n          requirements of UR I2 and UR I3 may be given the additional notation “Icebreaker”.\\n          “Icebreaker\\\" refers to any ship having an operational profile that includes escort or ice\\n          management functions, having powering and dimensions that allow it to undertake\\n          aggressive operations in ice-covered waters.\\n\\n          I1.1.4 For ships which are assigned a Polar Class notation, the hull form and propulsion\\n          power are to be such that the ship can operate independently and at continuous speed in a\\n          representative ice condition, as defined in Table 1 for the corresponding Polar Class. For\\n          ships and ship-shaped units which are intentionally not designed to operate independently in\\n          ice, such operational intent or limitations are to be explicitly stated in the Certificate of\\n          Classification or equivalent.\\n\\n          I1.1.5 For ships which are assigned a Polar Class notation PC 1 through PC 5, bows with\\n          vertical sides, and bulbous bows are generally to be avoided. Bow angles should in general\\n          be within the range specified in I2.3.1 (v).\\n\\n\\n          Note:\\n\\n          1.      UR I1 applies to ships contracted for construction on or after 1 July 2007.\\n\\n          2.      Rev.1 of this UR is to be uniformly applied by IACS Societies on ships contracted for\\n                  construction on and after 1 March 2008.\\n\\n          3.      Rev.2 of this UR is to be uniformly implemented by IACS Societies on ships contracted\\n                  for construction on and after 1 July 2017.\\n\\n          4.      The “contracted for construction” date means the date on which the contract to build the\\n                  vessel is signed between the prospective owner and the shipbuilder. For further details\\n                  regarding the date of “contract for construction”, refer to IACS Procedural Requirement\\n                  (PR) No. 29.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n                                                  I1-1                  IACS Req. 2006/Rev.2 2016\\n\\f                                                                                                        I1\\n\\n\\n         I1.1.6 For ships which are assigned a Polar Class notation PC 6 and PC 7, and are\\nI1       designed with a bow with vertical sides or bulbous bows, operational limitations (restricted\\n(cont)   from intentional ramming) in design conditions are to be stated in the Certificate of\\n         Classification or equivalent.\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/IACS_I1_Rev2_2016.txt\", \"edition\": \"Rev.2 (April 2016)\", \"authority\": \"IACS\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 0, \"end\": 3661, \"line_start\": 1, \"line_end\": 67, \"page_start\": 1, \"page_end\": 2}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E101\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#stage1LocalName> \\\"upperIceWaterline\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E102\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E103\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Lower ice waterline\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E104\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> \\\"P_min_UIWL_kW\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E105\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Batch 01 development): Has upper ice waterline is the benchmark representation of the linked requirement operand, relationship, evidence role, or controlled value. Exact scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E106\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLength> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#stage1LocalName> \\\"upperIceWaterlineLength\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E107\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#situatedAboveLowerIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E108\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#brashIceChannelResistanceAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Applicable TRAFICOM regulation wording plus explicit engineering node/operand role\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E109\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-020\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E110\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-012\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E111\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"Class\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Passenger ship\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"passengerShip\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"IMO-070 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.24 | 8.3.3.1.1; IMO-118 | IMO_POLAR_CODE p.43 | 4.2.2\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E112\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#brashIceChannelResistanceAtUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E113\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#benchmarkEntity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E114\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#cargoShip> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E115\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasLowerIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E116\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \\\"Minimum required power at upper ice waterline\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E117\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#displacementAtUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Displacement at upper ice waterline\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E118\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-016\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E119\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterlineReferencePosition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#roleDecisionBasis> \\\"Numeric operand, comparison value, formula input/output, or engineering measurement.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E120\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineBreadth> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#recommendedUnit> <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/M> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E121\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Unit-stripped normalized regulatory variable\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E122\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E123\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtLowerIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Minimum required power at lower ice waterline\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E124\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLengthLUI> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"I2-051\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E125\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#roleDecisionBasis> \\\"Quantity metadata requires the canonical QUDT QuantityValue node pattern\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E126\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> \\\"Passenger ship\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E127\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#changeNote> \\\"Retired in VOCAB-DEV-2026-08-13-BATCH01-R8.1-POSTCONFIRMATION: string representation cannot express the required Batch 01 node/value model.\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E128\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineDraughtDUI> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"I2-050\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E129\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#passengerShip> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#stage1LocalName> \\\"passengerShip\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E130\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Batch 01 development): Ice waterline is the benchmark representation of the linked requirement operand, relationship, evidence role, or controlled value. Exact scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E131\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#draftConceptId> \\\"VOC-0438\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E132\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineLength> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitSymbol> \\\"m\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E133\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE\", \"text\": \"         I2.3.2 Glancing impact load characteristics\\n\\n         The parameters defining the glancing impact load characteristics are reflected in the Class\\n         Factors listed in Table 1 and Table 2.\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n                                                I2-3                   IACS Req. 2006/Rev.4 2019\\n\\f                                                                                                                 I2\\n\\n\\n\", \"origin\": {\"file\": \"data/requirements/IACS_I2_full.txt\", \"edition\": \"Rev.4 (December 2019)\", \"authority\": \"IACS\", \"selection\": {\"start\": 7327, \"end\": 7750, \"line_start\": 142, \"line_end\": 154, \"page_start\": 3, \"page_end\": 4}}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E134\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#pleasureYacht> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"Not a quantity property\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E135\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#sourceRequirementId> \\\"TRF-020\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E136\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#upperIceWaterlineReferencePosition> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Applicable TRAFICOM regulation wording plus explicit engineering node/operand role\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E137\", \"kind\": \"SCHEMA_TEXT\", \"text\": \"{\\\"datatype\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"iri\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasLowerIceWaterline\\\", \\\"kind\\\": \\\"ObjectProperty\\\", \\\"label\\\": \\\"Has lower ice waterline\\\", \\\"localName\\\": \\\"hasLowerIceWaterline\\\", \\\"parentOrRange\\\": \\\"https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceWaterline\\\", \\\"sourceRefs\\\": \\\"TRF-012 | TRAFICOM p.6 | 2.1; TRF-013 | TRAFICOM p.7 | 2.2; TRF-020 | TRAFICOM p.8-9 | 3.2.2\\\", \\\"unitIri\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"unitSymbol\\\": \\\"\\\"}\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"schema_terms\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E138\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#lowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#roleDecisionBasis> \\\"Conservative textual scalar fallback\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E139\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#hasLowerIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Applicable TRAFICOM regulation wording plus explicit engineering node/operand role\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E140\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#brashIceChannelResistanceAtUpperIceWaterline> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \\\"NORMALIZED (Batch 01 development): Brash ice channel resistance at upper ice waterline is the benchmark representation of the linked requirement operand, relationship, evidence role, or controlled value. Exact scope is limited to the cited requirements.\\\"@en .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E141\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#brashIceChannelResistanceAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#unitDecisionStatus> \\\"No external unit IRI claimed; preserve the source unit in evidence\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E142\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#minimumRequiredPowerAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#roleDecisionBasis> \\\"Quantity metadata requires the canonical QUDT QuantityValue node pattern\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\", \"origin\": {\"context_field\": \"ontology_evidence\"}}, {\"evidence_id\": \"E143\", \"kind\": \"RDF_FACT\", \"text\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#displacementAtUpperIceWaterline> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#namingBasis> \\\"Benchmark-coined descriptive engineering term\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org